// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`buildSkillMarkdown > matches its snapshot 1`] = `
"---
name: enginecv
description: Edit the user's EngineCV resume file (an enginecv.authoring/v1 JSON document) safely. Use when the user asks you to add, change, remove or reorder content in their CV or resume file.
---

# EngineCV resume file

EngineCV (https://enginecv.app) is a resume builder that runs in the browser. The user's CV is linked to a JSON file on their computer. You edit that file with your normal file tools; the editor notices the change within a few seconds, checks it and updates the CV. If you do not know the file's path, ask the user for it.

> The file holds the user's CV, including contact details. Treat it as private: never copy it to a place the user did not ask for, and tell the user that reading it may send its contents to your model provider.

## The format

The file is one JSON document with \`"format": "enginecv.authoring/v1"\`. Schema: https://enginecv.app/schema/authoring/v1.json

Overview:

- format: "enginecv.authoring/v1" (required)
- design (optional hints): template, accent ("#rrggbb"), cvLanguage
- basics: name, headline, email, phone, location, website, linkedin, github, links, drivingLicense, nationality, dateOfBirth, passport, nationalId, maritalStatus, militaryService, genderPronoun, disability, visa, height
- summary: Markdown text
- experience[]: position, company, location, start, end, description, highlights, skills, url
- education[]: institution, studyType, area, location, start, end, score, description, courses, skills, url
- courses[]: name, institution, location, start, end, description, skills, url
- projects[]: name, subtitle, start, end, description, highlights, keywords, skills, url, repos, visibility
- organisations[]: name, role, location, start, end, description, skills, url
- certificates[]: name, issuer, date, description, skills, url, issuerUrl
- awards[]: name, issuer, date, description, skills, url
- publications[]: name, publisher, date, description, skills, url
- references[]: name, position, organisation, email, phone, description, url
- declaration: text, fullName, place, date
- skills: ["name", ...] or { "Group": ["name", { "name", "level" }] }; level: beginner, amateur, competent, proficient, expert
- languages: ["Language: level", ...]; level: A1–C2 or native
- interests: ["name", ...] or [{ name, description }]
- custom[]: { title, text } or { title, tags: [...] } or { title, entries: [{ title, subtitle, location, start, end, description, skills, url }] }

### \`basics\`

| Field | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| \`name\` | Full name. |
| \`headline\` | Short professional title under the name. |
| \`email\` | Email address, or a list of them. |
| \`phone\` | Phone number with country code. |
| \`location\` | City and country. |
| \`website\` | Personal website. |
| \`linkedin\` | LinkedIn profile URL. |
| \`github\` | GitHub profile URL. |
| \`links\` | Other profiles: [{ "name", "url", "label" }]. |
| \`drivingLicense\` | Driving licence categories, e.g. "B". |
| \`nationality\` | Nationality as an ISO country code ("BA") or a name. |
| \`dateOfBirth\` | Date of birth, only if the person wants it on the CV. |
| \`passport\` | Passport number, only if the person wants it on the CV. |
| \`nationalId\` | National ID number, only if the person wants it on the CV. |
| \`maritalStatus\` | Marital status, only if the person wants it on the CV. |
| \`militaryService\` | Military service status. |
| \`genderPronoun\` | Gender or pronouns. |
| \`disability\` | Disability status. |
| \`visa\` | Work permit or visa. |
| \`height\` | Height. |

### \`experience\` (list of entries)

| Field | Kind | Meaning |
| --- | --- | --- |
| \`id\` | id | Optional entry id. Keep ids you were given so entries can be matched later; never invent them. |
| \`position\` | text | Job title. |
| \`company\` | text | Employer. |
| \`location\` | text | City and/or country. |
| \`start\` | date | Start date. A date as "YYYY" or "YYYY-MM"; an end date still running is "present". Leave it out when unknown. |
| \`end\` | date | End date. A date as "YYYY" or "YYYY-MM"; an end date still running is "present". Leave it out when unknown. |
| \`description\` | markdown | Free text in Markdown (bold, italic, links, bullet lists). |
| \`highlights\` | highlights | Achievements, one short sentence each. |
| \`skills\` | list | Skills used here, as short names. |
| \`url\` | link | A link for this entry. |

### \`education\` (list of entries)

| Field | Kind | Meaning |
| --- | --- | --- |
| \`id\` | id | Optional entry id. Keep ids you were given so entries can be matched later; never invent them. |
| \`institution\` | text | School or university. |
| \`studyType\` | text | Degree or qualification, e.g. "Bachelor", "MSc". |
| \`area\` | text | Field of study. |
| \`location\` | text | City and/or country. |
| \`start\` | date | Start date. A date as "YYYY" or "YYYY-MM"; an end date still running is "present". Leave it out when unknown. |
| \`end\` | date | End date. A date as "YYYY" or "YYYY-MM"; an end date still running is "present". Leave it out when unknown. |
| \`score\` | text | Grade or GPA, as written on the diploma. |
| \`description\` | markdown | Free text in Markdown (bold, italic, links, bullet lists). |
| \`courses\` | list | Notable courses. |
| \`skills\` | list | Skills used here, as short names. |
| \`url\` | link | A link for this entry. |

